they give these  people a community they give them  something to bond around it  it recognizes the positive elements of  fandom while at the same time not  ignoring the sometimes sad elements of  fandom so I I think it strikes that  balance really well I think there's a  big part of why Star Trek fans tend to  like this a lot and you wouldn't  necessarily expect that because you know  fans don't like to be made fun of but  this doesn't feel like maybe funny it  feels this is the kind of humor that  feels like it's made by people who also  love this so it feels like it I don't  know a ton about the the writers of the  director if they are Trek fans but at  the very least they understood how to  approach that and portray that because  it it feels like the kind of send-up  that is done by somebody who genuinely  understands the material and understands  why people like it and why it's  important to them so that goes a long  way towards avoiding what could have  been some real cringy stuff and you know  when it makes fun of Star Trek and shows  like it it does so with legitimate  points and also just gently just ribbing  Lee look like pointing out that the  captain always ends up without a shirt  whenever he's fighting something and you  know all these sorts of things and the  other thing that helps is that it's not  uncommon for these sorts of satires to  get basically get underfunded and they  look cheap so you know you get a lot of  stuff with thats basically just ends up  being elevated fan films you know stuff  like this rarely gets a decent budget  but this does have a decent budget which  means the effects at the time it came  out we're on par with a legitimate  sci-fi film but it's a comedy it's a  parody and  best kind of parodies are always the  ones that at least visually match the  thing they're parody the more you can  look like the real thing the better the  comedy lands and this is able to do that  in a way that I would be surprised if it  ever happens again because try these did  trying to look like a legitimate Star  Wars or Marvel or DC or whatever film is  extremely expensive so the very idea of  of launching an original comedy with the  budget of a sci-fi film yo of a sci-fi  action film that's insane  but they did it here I'm really glad for  it this this is a movie that I laugh  every time and I often laugh at  different things every time and and the  god they cover the gamut with the stuff  that they they pick on right and right  down to the kid who piloted the ship as  a little jab at sort of the Wesley type  characters it's but again at the same  time not hateful jabbing a loving jab  because this is this is a this isn't a  takedown of Star Trek and Star Trek fans  it's a roast and it's the kind of roast  and you know forget fryers clapping you  know the the Comedy Central roasts crap  like that they're just trying to be as  cruel as possible but it's the kind of  roast that happens between friends  between people who know each other love  each other  love the same things but aren't above  just laughing about it because it's  important to be able to do that and if  you've never seen Galaxy Quest before do  like right away I I really strongly  recommend this film it's even separate  from its references the humor works much  in the same way something like airplane  or Blazing Saddles did even if you don't  know the tropes that they're picking  apart the jokes are funny in and of  themselves and you know the tropes it's  all the funnier so if you've never seen  it give it a watch if you have seen it  when was the last time you watched it  seriously I hadn't seen it in a few  years so it was  nice to have it be be brought up for  this so those are my thoughts on Galaxy  Quest have you seen it what did you  think about it whatever your thoughts  are drop something down the comments  let's talk about it there's a ton of  buttons down there too plus also links  for stuff such as my patreon and you  know check it 